{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# Blockchain — Hash Chain & Merkle Tree\n> Hedera Developer Course: Lectures 2 & 3 · See also [[wiki/concepts/blockchain-technology]] · [[wiki/concepts/cryptographic-hash-functions]]","x":0,"y":0,"width":800,"height":280},
		{"id":"anatomy-header","type":"text","text":"## 1 · Block Anatomy\nWhat fields go *into* the SHA-256 hash, and what comes out.","x":0,"y":360,"width":700,"height":220},
		{"id":"link-blockchain","type":"file","file":"wiki/concepts/blockchain-technology.md","x":960,"y":360,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"link-hash","type":"file","file":"wiki/concepts/cryptographic-hash-functions.md","x":960,"y":500,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"link-lecture2","type":"file","file":"wiki/sources/hedera-lecture-2-blockchain-hashing.md","x":960,"y":640,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"link-example","type":"file","file":"wiki/examples/hedera-local-ledger-js.md","x":960,"y":780,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"anatomy-fields","type":"text","text":"### Fields hashed (SHA-256 input)\n\n| Field | Example value |\n|-------|---------------|\n| `index` | `1` |\n| `data` | `{ type: \"TRANSFER\", amount: 10 }` |\n| `timestamp` | `2024-01-15T12:00:00.000Z` |\n| `prevHash` | `a3f7c8d2e19b4501...` |\n\n> ⚠ The block's own `hash` field is **excluded** — it is the *output*, not part of the input.\n\n```js\n// JavaScript trick (Lecture 2)\nconst { hash, ...rest } = block;\nreturn crypto.createHash('sha256')\n  .update(JSON.stringify(rest))\n  .digest('hex');\n```\n\n```java\n// Java equivalent (Lecture 2)\nMessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance(\"SHA-256\");\nbyte[] encoded = digest.digest(\n  (data + previousHash).getBytes());\n```","x":0,"y":660,"width":480,"height":930},
		{"id":"chain-header","type":"text","text":"## 2 · Hash Chain\nEach block stores the *hash* of the previous block as `prevHash`. Tampering with any block's data changes its hash, breaking the link to every block that follows.","x":0,"y":1670,"width":820,"height":260},
		{"id":"block-2","type":"text","text":"### Block 2\n\n`index` → **2**\n`data` → `{ amount: 5 }`\n`timestamp` → `2024-01-01T00:02:00Z`\n`prevHash` → `b91ac4f7d2e8c1a9` ↑\n\n---\n\n**`hash` → `c42de9a1bf3807cd`**","x":720,"y":2010,"width":280,"height":480,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"validation","type":"text","text":"### 3 · `isChainValid()` — O(n) Verification\n\n```js\nfor (let i = 1; i < chain.length; i++) {\n  const curr = chain[i];\n  const prev = chain[i - 1];\n\n  // Check 1: prevHash link intact?\n  if (curr.prevHash !== prev.hash)\n    return false;\n\n  // Check 2: block's own hash untampered?\n  if (curr.hash !== computeHash(curr))\n    return false;\n}\nreturn true; // every link verified\n```\n\nTwo checks per block pair: link integrity + self-integrity.","x":0,"y":2570,"width":460,"height":770,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"attack","type":"text","text":"### ⚠ Single-Chain Attack\n\nAttacker modifies **Block 1** `data`:\n\n```\nBlock 1 data changed\n  → Block 1 hash changes\n     → Block 2 prevHash ≠ Block 1 hash\n        → Block 2 hash changes\n           → Block 3 breaks … cascade\n```\n\n**Can the attacker recompute all hashes?**\nYes — on a *single* local copy. Hash chaining alone is not enough.\n\n**Defeated by distribution:**\nThousands of independent nodes each hold a copy. An attacker must recompute *and* overwrite the majority simultaneously:\n- Bitcoin: must control >50% of global hash power (PoW)\n- Ethereum: must control >⅓ of staked ETH (PoS)\n- Hedera: ABFT — mathematically impossible with <⅓ malicious nodes","x":540,"y":2570,"width":460,"height":870,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"colour-legend","type":"text","text":"**Legend**\n\n🟡 Genesis block\n🔵 Chain blocks\n🟢 Hash output / Merkle Root\n🔴 Attack / warning\n🟠 Leaf hashes\n🟣 Raw transactions","x":1080,"y":2570,"width":220,"height":450},
		{"id":"merkle-header","type":"text","text":"## 4 · Merkle Tree (inside each block)\nTransactions are hashed in pairs up a binary tree. The **Merkle Root** is stored in the block header. Change any single transaction → root changes → block header hash changes → chain broken.","x":0,"y":3520,"width":820,"height":260},
		{"id":"merkle-root","type":"text","text":"### 🌳 Merkle Root\n\n`H( H₁₂ ‖ H₃₄ )`\n`= 9f3ab21c8e4d7b05...`\n\n📦 Stored in block header\n(proves all 4 transactions\nwithout storing them here)","x":360,"y":3860,"width":240,"height":380,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"h12","type":"text","text":"**H₁₂**\n`H( H₁ ‖ H₂ )`\n`= 4a7bc39f8d21...`","x":130,"y":4320,"width":200,"height":230,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"h34","type":"text","text":"**H₃₄**\n`H( H₃ ‖ H₄ )`\n`= 8e2df17a3c90...`","x":630,"y":4320,"width":200,"height":230,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"merkle-proof","type":"text","text":"### Merkle Proof — Audit Efficiency\n\nTo prove **Tx1 is in this block**, a verifier only needs:\n\n1. `H₁` = SHA-256(Tx1)\n2. `H₂` (sibling)\n3. `H₃₄` (uncle subtree root)\n4. Compare recomputed `H(H₁₂ ‖ H₃₄)` against the Merkle Root\n\n**Cost: log₂(n) hashes** instead of all n transactions.\n\n| Transactions | Hashes needed for proof |\n|---|---|\n| 4 | 2 |\n| 1,000 | ~10 |\n| 1,000,000 | ~20 |\n\nUsed by Bitcoin SPV (Simplified Payment Verification) and Ethereum light clients.","x":1020,"y":4320,"width":360,"height":800,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"h1","type":"text","text":"**H₁**\n`SHA-256(Tx1)`\n`= 1a2b3c4d...`","x":20,"y":4630,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"h2","type":"text","text":"**H₂**\n`SHA-256(Tx2)`\n`= 4d5e6f7a...`","x":270,"y":4630,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"h3","type":"text","text":"**H₃**\n`SHA-256(Tx3)`\n`= 7b8c9d1e...`","x":520,"y":4630,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"h4","type":"text","text":"**H₄**\n`SHA-256(Tx4)`\n`= 2f3a4b5c...`","x":770,"y":4630,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"tx1","type":"text","text":"**Tx 1**\nAlice → Bob\n2 HBAR","x":20,"y":4940,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"tx2","type":"text","text":"**Tx 2**\nBob → Carol\n1 HBAR","x":270,"y":4940,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"tx3","type":"text","text":"**Tx 3**\nCarol → Dave\n0.5 HBAR","x":520,"y":4940,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"tx4","type":"text","text":"**Tx 4**\nDave → Alice\n3 HBAR","x":770,"y":4940,"width":170,"height":230,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"anatomy-output","type":"text","text":"### Hash output (SHA-256)\n\n```\nInput:   any size (1 byte → ∞)\nOutput:  256 bits = 32 bytes\n         = 64 hex characters\n\nExample output:\nb91ac4f7d2e8c1a9\n3f05b8d7a4291e6c\n...(always exactly 64 chars)\n```\n\n**Four secure properties:**\n1. **Data Integrity** — 1-bit change → ~50% output flips (avalanche)\n2. **One-Way** — cannot reverse the hash to find input\n3. **Collision Resistant** — cannot find two inputs with same output\n4. **Fixed Output** — always 256 bits regardless of input size","x":920,"y":710,"width":320,"height":830,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"extends","type":"text","text":"**Block 4, 5, 6 … →**\n\nChain grows indefinitely. Every new block anchors cryptographically to the previous one.","x":1720,"y":2090,"width":220,"height":320},
		{"id":"block-3","type":"text","text":"### Block 3\n\n`index` → **3**\n`data` → `{ amount: 2 }`\n`timestamp` → `2024-01-01T00:03:00Z`\n`prevHash` → `c42de9a1bf3807cd` ↑\n\n---\n\n**`hash` → `d85f2c3e7419b8fa`**","x":1360,"y":2010,"width":280,"height":480,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"block-genesis","type":"text","text":"### Genesis Block\n\n`index` → **0**\n`data` → `{}`\n`timestamp` → `2024-01-01T00:00:00Z`\n`prevHash` → `0000000000000000`\n\n---\n\n**`hash` → `a3f7c8d2e19b4501`**","x":-680,"y":2010,"width":280,"height":480,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"block-1","type":"text","text":"### Block 1\n\n`index` → **1**\n`data` → `{ amount: 10 }`\n`timestamp` → `2024-01-01T00:01:00Z`\n`prevHash` → `a3f7c8d2e19b4501` ↑\n\n---\n\n**`hash` → `b91ac4f7d2e8c1a9`**","x":0,"y":2010,"width":280,"height":480,"color":"5"}
	],
